  "verbalization": "Quiquesetinerviusin B appears to have a complex relationship with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target interactions. The evidence suggests that Quiquesetinerviusin B acts as a target for Caspase-2, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Deoxyaconitine, GlyTouCan:G87587VQ, and 6alpha-Hydroxycleroda-3,13-dien-16,15-olid-18-oic acid. These compounds all ultimately target Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a potential pathway where Quiquesetinerviusin B may influence the activity of Caspase-2, which then modulates Phosphodiesterase 6C. The shared target relationship between Caspase-2 and Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a possible regulatory mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where Quiquesetinerviusin B may function as a modulator of Caspase-2, which in turn affects Phosphodiesterase 6C, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this mechanism.",
